    Split the Prepare header's menu into this project and the app

    The ⋯ menu now follows the main-10-prepare-header-project-menu board.
    First this project: a name row (the name in Body Bold, the save state on
    the right, a chevron) that opens the Project tab, then Version history
    and Export project 3MF…. Then a hairline, Preferences… with its
    shortcut, a hairline, and Switch to classic view…. The unclickable
    title row, Recent projects… and Back to Prepare are gone. The autosave
    warning rows still sit directly under the name row. The name row and
    Version history switch to Prepare and open the pane if it is
    collapsed; Export runs the pane's export without opening it.

    Tab on the Prepare canvas no longer flips to OrcaSlicer's Preview: the
    shell takes EVT_GLCANVAS_TAB there and drops it, and gives it back when
    it is removed. OrcaSlicer's Ctrl+R still reaches Preview.

    A model file that starts a project (OS open, Home's Open…, a Home
    drop) goes into OrcaSlicer's File › Recent files. Zip archives and
    Home's temporary dropped copies are left out. Choosing a model file
    from Recent files now opens it as a new project, like an OS open, by
    sending non-3MF paths in the external project open handler to
    take_opened_files.

    Menu hairlines in every HeaderMenu were wxStaticLine, which Windows
    draws in its own grey whatever colour it is given. They are now a
    filled strip in border-subtle, one outline width thick, inset 12 DIP
    like the row labels.

    The Slice split button showed short hard lines on its top and bottom
    edges where its halves meet. Each half squared its inner corners with a
    patch on whole pixels over a rounded rectangle drawn half a pixel in,
    so the patch filled the edge rows the rectangle only half covers. Each
    half now extends its rounded rectangle two radii past the seam, as the
    printer chip's halves do, and draws no patch.

    All changes are in fork-owned files under src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/.
    The shell harness checks the new rows, order, name row decoration,
    Tab staying on Prepare (also after each return from classic view),
    the retry row's place when storage is unavailable, and Recent files;
    --left-pane-capture also saves the open menu. On Windows the default
    mode shows only its six known failures; --file-opening,
    --classic-switch and --unavailable-storage pass.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
